      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Thuliasaur Island [zone=1020]\n**Who:**\n- Galeth Veredeth [npc=47726]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 105\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Related Zones:**\n- Thuliasaur Island: Fit For the New World [zone=1032]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Galeth Veredeth [npc=48606]\n- Lyirae Oakwynd [npc=48607]\n- Praetor Venatos [npc=48608]\n- Thuliasaur [npc=48609]\n- Una Lucem [npc=48610]\n- a bulwark [npc=48590]\n- a burner [npc=48591]\n- a chest - Fit For the New World [npc=48689]\n- a healer [npc=48592]\n- a razer [npc=48593]\n- a reaver [npc=48594]\n- a salver [npc=48595]\n- a scout [npc=48596]\n- a slaughterer [npc=48597]\n- a snarer [npc=48598]\n- a squad leader [npc=48599]\n- a trapper [npc=48600]\n- a vanguard [npc=48601]\n**Related Quests:**\n- TDS Progression #0: An Overview [quest=7701]\n- TDS Progression #15: To Remake Eden [quest=7717]\n- TDS Progression #17: A Fickle Wind Blows [quest=7719]\n**Era:** | !The Darkened Sea\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 3\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Sun Oct 26 02:58:19 2014\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 |\n---\n\n**The Darkened Sea Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This group mission begins with Galeth Veredeth ( **click for map image**) on Thuliasaur Island._\n_Pre-Requisites for Requesting:_\n\\- Completion of \"A Rising Storm\" (Tempest Temple)\n\\- Completion of \"Gathering Clouds\" (Tempest Temple)\n\\- Completion of \"Clearer Skies\" (Tempest Temple)\n\\- Completion of \"The Edge of Balance\" (Katta Castrum: Deluge)\n\\- Completion of \"The Abscent Scholar\" (Katta Castrum: Deluge)\n\\- Completion of \"Just Recompense\" (Brother Island)\n\\- Completion of \"The Cover of Night\" (Brother Island)\n\\- Completion of \"Loyal is the Heart\" (Caverns of Endless Song)\n\\- Completion of \"Leave No Brother Behind\" (Caverns of Endless Song)\n\\- Completion of \"Two Sides of the Shield\" (Caverns of Endless Song)\n\\- Completion of \"The Sacred Profaned\" (Degmar, the Lost Castle)\n\\- Completion of \"Crying for the Dead\" (Degmar, the Lost Castle)\n\\- Completion of \"Burden of the Past\" (Degmar, the Lost Castle)\n\\- Completion of \"An Endless Cycle\" (Thuliasaur Island)\n\\- Completion of \"To Remake Eden\" (Thuliasaur Island)\n_Say \"stop\" to request the mission and \"proceed\" to zone in._\nYou say, 'Hail, Galeth Veredeth'\nGaleth Veredeth says 'The [search] has taught us much. Now it is the [moment] to [stop] the enemy.'\nYou say, 'The moment?'\nGaleth Veredeth watches a stick insect slowly crawling across his metal hand. 'Time moves so swiftly here... I forgot the urgency of the mortal. When I see the rain falling and the creatures creeping, or I hear the clicks of my clockwork gears, they all rush [together].\nYou say, 'Together?'\nGaleth Veredeth says 'We spirits gather here for but a short time. The ones who have known nothing but the mortal cannot see how swiftly it travels, and they fear the vastness of time beyond their flesh. Lyirae feels this fear. She wishes to fight alone, thinking to [protect] me from the vastness.'\nYou say, 'Protect you?'\nGaleth Veredeth says 'Each of us will pass from the river to the sea. Some quibble over time, but all mortals reach it in a blink. Lyirae should not protect me. She should look to the stream. Protect the flow, the current upon which all time is carried.' Galeth touches a leaf and allows the stick insect to crawl from his hand. 'Time is both infinite and short. Let us [stop] the enemy.'\nYou say, 'We'll stop them...'\nGaleth Veredeth says 'The enemy forces amass on the beach. Any moment they will march into the jungle. \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_, Lyirae fears the inevitable: the abandonment of flesh and the infinity of spirit. Let us give her no cause to fear for us. [Proceed] now. We will face them together.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Fit for the New World'.\nThe Combine are trying to capture a large creature on the island. They are about to send reinforcements, and Galeth thinks this is the time to stop them.\nYou say, 'Let's proceed'\nGaleth Veredeth says 'Indeed.'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Thuliasaur Island.\n\n---\n\n!\n\n---\n\nSpeak with Galeth 0/3 (Thuliasaur Island)\n_Hail him three times for the update, and then watch out because a group of mobs makes its way towards the area from the south (they do not see invisibility)._\nGaleth Veredeth says 'Lyirae could not wait. She told me to stay behind. She has followed a line of reinforcements pushing into the interior. Still my joints constrain me, and I could not keep up with her pace.'\nGaleth Veredeth says 'Lyirae thought I would be easy prey with my current capabilities of locomotion.' Galeth wheezes through his steam vents, which sounds almost like laughter. 'She is kind for worrying about the fate of a spirit inside a metal body.''\nGaleth Veredeth says 'She would have cause for sadness if we did not move south. Other groups of reinforcements have landed on the shore and begin to push north. We must cut them off.'\n\n---\n\nDefeat the landing party marching northward 0/13 (Thuliasaur Island)\n_Average difficulty mobs, but have a fair amount of hitpoints and are fairly close together. They are mezzable and rootable/snareable. If you aggro and fade \"a squad leader\" after having killed a few troops, they may respawn. This doesn't matter, though, as any 13 of these mobs will update and progress the task._\n_Upon killing the last one, you see:_\nGaleth Veredeth says 'We should find Lyirae. The soldiers are not the only ones deserving of reinforcements. She followed them to the northwest.'\n\n---\n\nSpeak with Lyirae on the southern hill facing the western river branch 0/4 (Thuliasaur Island)\n_She is found along the western boundary of the raptor area (no raptors in the instanced version of the zone, but it's in the same area)._\nLyirae Oakwynd shouts 'What are you doing here, Galeth? The rain -- you'll grind to a halt and get yourself killed!'\nGaleth Veredeth shouts 'You forget I am a spirit of Growth. I cannot die like you imagine. This metal body...'\nLyirae Oakwynd fires another arrow through the rain, keeping the Combine squad pinned down. 'You're here now. I can see you, touch you, hear you. If you were far away and I could not see your fate, perhaps it would be different. But nothing will happen to you under my watch!'\nGaleth Veredeth readies his sword. 'I could say the same. I will not let your life spill into the sea just yet. Keep them occupied.' Galeth rushes toward the Combine squad.\nLyirae Oakwynd shouts 'Galeth! Adventurers, help him!'\nGaleth Veredeth's arm slows as he swings his sword. His joints grind and freeze as he turns to parry a strike.\nDefeat the Combine squad 0/10 (Thuliasaur Island)\n_These mobs are of the same variety as previous._\nSpeak with Lyirae 0/3 (Thuliasaur Island)\nLyirae Oakwynd looks ruefully at Galeth. 'I told you this would happen...'\nGaleth Veredeth manages to lower his arm a few inches. 'I should have a word with Ognit about the quality of his craftsmanship...'\nLyirae Oakwynd pours a small flask of plant oil onto Galeth's joints and tries to loosen them.\nSpeak with Galeth 0/3 (Thuliasaur Island)\nGaleth Veredeth's arms and legs start to move more freely. 'I can keep going, but I don't know how much longer my body will be useful in this rain.'\nLyirae Oakwynd yells, 'Galeth, stay here! I don't want to see you destroyed today!' Lyirae runs further into the forest.\nGaleth Veredeth says, 'Though my body slows I shall not abandon her.'\n\n---\n\nMove west, up the river to Lyirae 0/1 (Thuliasaur Island)\nLyirae Oakwynd frowns as she hears the clanking of Galeth's approach. 'He is going to get himself killed...'\nLyirae Oakwynd points to the group of nearby Combine. 'Do you see them slaughtering the creatures? What are they doing? Those creatures have done nothing... we must stop this!'\nDefeat the Combine squad 0/11 (Thuliasaur Island)\n_Same as above. Upon the last kill, you see:_\nGaleth Veredeth points westward down the river. 'This is just the bait. There are older, larger things that lurk in the sea.'\n\n---\n\nReach the clearing at the end of the river to the west 0/1 (Thuliasaur Island)\nSpeak with Galeth 0/10 (Thuliasaur Island)\nGaleth Veredeth raises his hand to you. 'Hold and listen.'\nPraetor Venatos shouts 'The stench of these creatures is enough to lure every fly from Odus! Una better arrive soon or she'll be late to supper!'\nUna Lucem's eyes wander around the forest, adjusting to the dim light. She does not blink as the rain strikes her pupils. Her gaze comes to rest on the mound of corpses. 'Looks like the courtyard after training. But these have all their pieces.'\nUna Lucem stares at Venatos. He looks at the ground. 'Where's the giant? Father said to fetch a giant.'\nGaleth Veredeth keeps looking at the ground. 'It's sure to come soon... we killed so many... and the stench will surely attract the beast...'\nUna Lucem cocks her head, still looking at Venatos. 'You didn't finish setting the plate.' With a swing of Una's sword, a shockwave fans out and cleaves the skin of the remaining dinosaurs.\nLyirae Oakwynd whispers to you and Galeth. 'She's a monster, just like the others!' Lyirae nocks an arrow and looses it at Una.\nUna Lucem , without more than a glance, flashes her sword like lightning amid the raindrops. Lyirae's arrow falls in twain. Una's eyes stare into the forest's gloom, marking the arrow's genesis.\nLyirae Oakwynd silently springs to action, darting through the undergrowth without a word, running at Una Lucem.\nGaleth Veredeth shouts, 'Lyirae!' Galeth clangs after her.\n\n---\n\nSpeak with Una Lucem 0/9 (Thuliasaur Island)\n**TASK LOCKS HERE**\n_Upon the ninth hail, be ready for a fight._\nUna Lucem emits a blast of magic, throwing Galeth and Lyirae to the ground. Galeth's frame and leg joints crack.\nUna Lucem looks at you impassively. 'You came to see me again. You must admire me.'\nPraetor Venatos glances around as the ground begins to shake. 'The creature is coming!'\nUna Lucem keeps looking at you. 'I see what father meant about weakness. The old races aren't as strong as I am. Their skin always burns off too quickly, or their limbs won't stay on.'\nPraetor Venatos cries out. Tree limbs snap as a gigantic lizard crashes into the clearing. As it lands, it crushes Venatos and his troops.\nPraetor Venatos died.\na vanguard died.\na razer died.\na scout died.\nUna Lucem raises her head to look up at the lizard towering above her. 'This one looks stronger. It will please Father.' Una Lucem begins casting a spell.\nLyirae Oakwynd calls out weakly. 'No, you must stop her! The creature is innocent...'\nUna Lucem turns her attention upon you. 'Yes? Why do you pester me? I am doing the good will of my father. He wants to bring perfection to the world. You don't want that? You don't want your children to have the strength of this creature? See how strong it is!'\nUna Lucem releases a spell upon the creature. It glares at you hungrily.\n\n---\n\nDefeat the Thuliasaur 0/1 (Thuliasaur Island)\n_Thuliasaur summons from 100% health; sees through all forms of invisibility; hits for a max ~24,500; AE rampages; single-target rampages; and has an AE called \"Massive Stomp\":_\nMassive Stomp: PB AE 100', Magic (-975)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 60000\n2: Stun (3.00 sec)\n_DPS it to 5% for the update._\nSee what happens to the Thuliasaur 0/1 (Thuliasaur Island)\nLyirae Oakwynd shouts 'No, don't kill it!'\nUna Lucem touches her fingers to the symbol on her breastplate. 'Oh, this creature is weak. It will never please Father.' She outstretches her other arm and points two fingers at the lizard. She drops her fingers toward the ground.\nFor a moment, the lizard is lit by a faint blue glow before a pillar of magic streaks out of the sky and consumes it.\nLyirae Oakwynd cries out and covers her head as the magical flames destroy the lizard and singe the trees.\nThuliasaur died.\nUna Lucem looks at you and blinks. 'I must meet Father's dark woman at the Dredge. You will come and watch me?' Una Lucem disappears in a pillar of light.\n\n---\n\nSpeak with Lyirae 0/5 (Thuliasaur Island)\n_Hail her until the task completes. A chest also spawns at this time. The task is repeatable with a 6-hour lockout timer from the time of request._\nLyirae Oakwynd puts her hand over the rent running down the front of Galeth's frame. 'I won't add to the salt... I don't want to ruin your joints...' Lyirae brushes her cheeks, though the rain still falls.\nLyirae Oakwynd looks at Galeth's legs, which have broken off below the knee joints. 'I knew this would happen... I told you to wait. This is how it always ends...'\nGaleth Veredeth's face remains expressionless as always. 'You know my metal feels no pain. And still my spirit lives. Take heart, Lyirae. We must go to Firiona. There is still time before we reach the sea.'\nLyirae Oakwynd picks up Galeth and bears his weight as best she can. She turns toward the beach. 'We will journey with you to Firiona, though...' Lyirae looks around at the burning stumps, the carcasses, and then the untouched jungle. 'I almost wish I could stay here -- remove myself from all the strife to come, all the death...'\nLyirae Oakwynd listens to Galeth speak as he rests on her back. 'As I said, there is still time. Our courses do not end on this island, in this river. We have a long way to go once we [leave] here. We should meet with Captain Sedgethwait on Brother Island and set sail together.\n_Rewards:_\n150 platinum\nExperience (3-4% of Level 105)\n_Possible Chest Loot (1 item + 0-1 armor templates + 0-1 Briny Essence + 0-1 Valiant ornament):_\nBlood Raven Mask\nGuard of the Blood Raven\nRaptor Bone Ring\nTemple Raider's Cloak\nWingblade\nHighwater Armguards\nHighwater Boots\nHighwater Bracer\nHighwater Gloves\nHighwater Helm\nHighwater Leggings\nHighwater Tunic\nMedian Briny Essence\nGreater Briny Essence\nGlowing Briny Essence",
