      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Thuliasaur Island [zone=1020]\n**Who:**\n- Historian Fjilnauk [npc=47727]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 105\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n- Faction\n- Money\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Faction Required:**\nThe Kromtus (Min: Apprehensive)\n**Factions Raised:**\n- The Kromtus +100\n**Factions Lowered:**\n**Quest Items:**\n- Anachronistic Kromtus Runestone [item=120456]\n- Ancient Kromtus Longsword [item=120460]\n- Battered Kromtus Shield [item=120457]\n- Hoary Tome of the Tribes [item=120459]\n- Worn Kromtus Helm [item=120458]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Frostcrypt, Throne of the Shade King [zone=443]\n- Goru`kar Mesa [zone=434]\n- Icefall Glacier [zone=438]\n- The Steppes [zone=437]\n- Valdeholm [zone=439]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- The Spirit of Hjirvlauk [npc=48177]\n- a restless shade [npc=48122]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Kromtus #1: Honoring the Elders [quest=7772]\n- Kromtus #2: Recovering Our History [quest=7773]\n**Era:** | !The Darkened Sea\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Sun Oct 26 03:58:12 2014\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 |\n---\n\n**The Darkened Sea Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This solo task is the third in a series of three. It begins with Historian Fjilnauk ( **click for map image**) on Thuliasaur Island._\n_Pre-Requisites for Requesting:_\n\\- Minimum Level 95\n\\- Minimum apprehensive faction with The Kromtus\n\\- Completed \"Honoring the Elders\"\n\\- Completed \"Recovering Our History\"\n_Say \"willing\" to request the task._\nYou say, 'Hail, Historian Fjilnauk'\nHistorian Fjilnauk says '\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_, I am honored to see you again. I believe it is time I share the intent of my work here. You see, in additional to adhering to the tenet of strict pacifism, our tribe has forbidden all form of written language. Our entire history for several generations has been passed down from elder to child. I fear this means that much of our storied past has been lost. The memory of the elders grows ever more distant each day. I would not defy our laws by scribing what I know to stone but I do suspect there is much that can be learned if any lost artifacts of our tribe can be recovered. I humbly request, if you are [willing], that you set out in search of these relics and return them to me so that I can decipher what the elders cannot recall.''\nYou say, 'Yes, I am willing...'\nHistorian Fjilnauk says 'If any artifacts of our people still exist they will probably rest in the hands of other tribes. I cannot say where this may be, but someone as well traveled as you probably has a few ideas of where to start.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Memories of the Kromtus'.\nHistorian Fjilnauk needs you to travel to the lands where the tribes of giants once united in service to Rallos and recover any artifact that may have belonged to the Kromtus clan.\nThe Dromrek clan that dwells in Goru`kar Mesa are among the most violent and simple giant tribes on Antonica. Scour their caves and see if anything out of the ordinary turns up.\nIn the foothills of Icefall Glacier in the lands called the Steppes there is an old Krithgorian burial site. Search the site for any relics that bear symbology foreign to the Krithgor clan.\nOnce you reach the gates of Valdeholm in Icefall Glacier, take note of the totems that stand on opposite sides of the narrow valley leading into the city. These monuments to Rallos are often constructed out of weapons and armor of fallen warriors. See if you can spot anything that might have belonged to the Kromtus clan.\nAt the far north end of the city of Valedholm you will find King Odeen's manor. Search the king's library for anything that may have some written history about our people.\nBelow the city of Valdeholm are the treacherous catacombs of their ancient dead. Take care as you delve deeper into this burial site. Look for the frozen Warlord as he oversees a small arena of battle. Search the statue's feet for any relic that has resisted the bitter cold.\n\n---\n\n_Map points for The Serpent's Spine map files:_\n_\"mesa.txt\":_\nP -2020.0000, -50.0000, 9.0000, 0, 127, 127, 1, relic\n_\"steppes.txt\":_\nP 3.0000, -2580.0000, 160.0000, 0, 127, 127, 1, relic\n_\"icefall.txt\":_\nP 130.0000, -2310.0000, 705.0000, 0, 127, 127, 1, relic\n_\"valdeholm.txt\":_\nP 985.0000, -3880.0000, 475.0000, 0, 127, 127, 1, relic\n_\"frostcrypt.txt\":_\nP 365.0000, -1470.0000, -129.0000, 0, 127, 127, 1, relic\n\n---\n\n!\n!\n!\n!\n!\n\n---\n\nUnearth a Kromtus Runestone 0/1 (Goru`Kar Mesa)\n_Head to Goru`Kar Mesa and find a stone at /loc 50, 2020, 9. Click it to receive an \"Anachronistic Kromtus Runestone\"._\nYou examine the runestone that sits precariously balanced on the stalagmite in the center of the cave. It has faded with age but you make out depictions of trees, blades and shields along with some text written in a language you can't quite make out. You pick up the runestone in hopes that it is in fact one of the Kromtus Relics.\nRecover a Kromtus Shield 0/1 (The Steppes)\n_Head to the Steppes and find a shield at /loc 2580, -3, 160. Click it to receive a \"Battered Kromtus Shield\"._\nA battered shield sits discarded in the corner. Upon closer inspection you make out several inscriptions that have been marred by the wear of heavy battle, 'For one who will march while cowards hide and fall where heroes lie.' You hoist the large shield onto your back, assured that this is one of the ancient Kromtus relics.\nObtain a Kromtus Helm 0/1 (Icefall Glacier)\n_Head to Icefall Glacier and find a helmet at /loc 2310, -130, 705 (on top of the eastern totem). Click it to receive a \"Worn Kromtus Helm\"._\nA giant's helmet sits half buried in snow at the top of this monument. Its age is hardly apparent upon inspection due to the magnificence of its construction. The metal, though heavily dented, shines pristinely. You brace yourself against the stone monument below and pull with all of your might and are able to dislodge the ancient piece of armor from the snow.\nBorrow a Tome of the Tribes 0/1 (Valdeholm)\n_Head to Valdeholm and find some books at /loc 3880, -985, 475. Click them to receive \"Hoary Tome of the Tribes\". This item is on top of one of the bookshelves. You might want to use levitate + a mount of some sort to get close enough to it._\nYou look up at the stack of tomes that rests atop the bookshelf, lodged between two volumes on royal lineage is a tome entitled, 'On the Tribes That Marched'. You pull the book down and look over the first few pages. You soon realize that the short tome gives a detailed account of every giant clan in Rallos' army at the time of his invasion on the Rathe. This will clearly be of interest to Historian Fjilnauk.\nExhume a Kromtus Longsword 0/1 (Frostcrypt, Throne of the Shade King)\n_Head to Frostcrypt and find a sword at /loc 1470, -365, -129. Click on it to receive \"Ancient Kromtus Longsword\". As with the Valdeholm update, you'll probably need a levitate effect or Rocketeer Boots to reach it. It's a giant sword on the statue's immediate east side._\nTo the side of the frozen statue of the Warlord sits a sword somehow kept in pristine condition. Shining runes are cut into the blade just above the hilt, their pattern matches other Kromtus relics that you have come across. You look around the room to ensure you are not being watched then carefully take the blade down from its resting place.\n\n---\n\nBring the Kromtus Runestone to Historian Fjilnauk 0/1 (Thuliasaur Island)\nBring the Kromtus Shield to Historian Fjilnauk 0/1 (Thuliasaur Island)\nBring the Kromtus Helm to Historian Fjilnauk 0/1 (Thuliasaur Island)\nBring the Tome of the Tribes to Historian Fjilnauk 0/1 (Thuliasaur Island)\nBring the Kromtus Longsword to Historian Fjilnauk 0/1 (Thuliasaur Island)\nHistorian Fjilnauk looks upon the artifacts you have presented him in disbelief. He speaks with renewed excitement, 'Simply incredible! To finally know our tribe once tread upon so much of the world. These instruments of war speak to a time when we were strong, capable of winning wars and toppling nations. This tome speaks of a proud lineage of generals, elders whose lives ended on the field of battle rather than withering away in solitude.' The giant pauses then looks to the west, 'Something stirs near the village square. You should investigate, small one.'\nAn elder giant spirit has taken form in the center of town. Step closer to learn of its purpose.\n\n---\n\nListen to the ancient Kromtus spirit 0/1 (Thuliasaur Island)\n_Task Window Says:_ An old Kromtus spirit has taken form in the center of town. Stand in its presence and listen to what it has to say. Should the spirit be preoccupied by another or you fail to heed its words, return to Historian Fjilnauk and speak to him to have the spirit make a new appearance.\n_Upon turning in all five items, \"The Spirit of Hjirvlauk\" a short distance southwest of the Historian. Stand near it while it tells a story, and be prepared for mob aggro. Soon, 1x \"a restless shade\" spawns and attack (max hit ~17,000; immune to mez; but is rootable/snareable; five-minute timer to kill). Soon after its death, another 2x \"a restless shade\" spawn and attack (same abilities; 8-minute timer to kill)._\n_If you fail the encounter or otherwise leave it idle after having spawned it, you can hail the Historian to respawn it. The same applies if you're having to wait for another player to do it._\n_Failure to kill the ambush mobs within their timers will cause the encounter to reset._\nYou need to be closer to the ancient giant's spirit to hear it.\nThe giant looks down at you, its ethereal face contorted in an expression of remorse. Without moving its mouth its voice consumes your thoughts, but he speaks in words you do not understand.\nIn your mind you see the Kromtus runestone, it is affixed to a battered suit of armor that rests upon the chest of a mighty warrior. The sky behind the warrior is blood red. The shouting of battle begins to overtake your ears right before the vision is lost.\nThe giant spirit's voice continues speaking to you and suddenly images of the now battered Kromtus shield coalesce into something lucid. The shield appears to you, unmarred with battle scars. It sits with several identical replicas in an armory. Your vision turns from the armory to several orcs that stand nearby. You quickly shake your head and regain sight of the land you stand in.\nThe spirit begins to move its hands in an elaborate gesture before calming its motions and drawing its fingers over the top of its head. You think back to the snow covered helmet you unearthed in Icefall Glacier atop the Valdeholm post.\nSuddenly a second spirit takes form. This one does not appear to be as friendly!\na restless shade says 'Die coward!'\na restless shade has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\na restless shade says 'Soon...'\nThat giant's attention returns to you, its gestures now smooth. Its foreign words carry a friendlier tone, it seems to be thankful. It continues to speak at length but little makes sense. Of all its words the only syllables that stick with you are what sounds like a name, 'Hjirvlauk?. You repeat the name, 'Hjirvlauk' and the shade nods slowly.\nThe spirit holds out its tightly clenched right fist. It places its left fist over it and moves its left arm up slowly, as if expressing the shape of a blade. He swings his right hand to the side and points the imaginary blade toward the sky. His disembodied voice turns to a shout then to heartfelt laughter and finally a sigh.\nThe spirit's gestures are suddenly interrupted by two voices, shouting in unison in common tongue!\na restless shade shouts, 'Hjirvlauk!'\na restless shade says 'Our blood is on your hands!'\na restless shade has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\na restless shade says 'Death is no escape.'\na restless shade has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\na restless shade says 'Narikor will soon claim you!'\nThe spirit of Hjirvlauk takes a final look around the village of giants that appear oblivious to his presence then returns his attention to you. A sense of mutual respect resonates between the two of you. He holds out his hand and points toward the Kromtus historian that remains enraptured by Hjirvlauk's earthly artifacts. The spirit nods, its disembodied voice now simply a whisper in your mind as it says its last word and the first word you are able to make sense of, 'Peace'.\n\n---\n\nSpeak to Historian Fjilnauk 0/1 (Thuliasaur Island)\n_Task Window Says:_ Return to Historian Fjilnauk to tell him what you have learned from the shade of Hjirvlauk.\nYou say, 'Hail, Historian Fjilnauk'\nHistorian Fjilnauk listens intently as you recount the elaborate pageantry of Hjirvlauk's spirit and the harrowing battle of the enraged undead. The historian remains stoic as his expression changes from interest to wonder as if a great revelation has just dawned upon him. He speaks, turning his attention to the nearest elder then back to you, 'Everything you have told me suggests that we did in fact march proudly in the Warlord's army and now suffer for it. Yet we possess the capacity to recover while others do not. Yes, our elders forbade written language and violence for this very reason, so that we could escape the cycle of war. Small one, I have no treasures great enough to express the depths of my gratitude for what you have shown me today. Please, accept this humble offering and know that I am eternally grateful for your help.'\nIt seems the elders' refusal to pass on the tribe's history to successive generations may have been an intentional one. Historian Fjilnauk will have to reflect upon whether or not he truly wishes to preserve the tribe's past.\n_Rewards:_\nFaction with The Kromtus (+68)\n--AND--\nTiny Parrot's Furcula --OR-- 100 platinum\n_This task is repeatable with a 6-hour lockout timer from the time of request._\n- Tiny Parrot's Furcula [item=120461]",
