      },
      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Thuliasaur Island [zone=1020]\n**Who:**\n- Silwat Viltor [ _Quests_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 105\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Quest Items:**\n- Discolored Swordfish Blood [item=120463]\n- Riverweed [item=119725]\n- Simple Antibody Concoction [item=120464]\n- Unusual Tortoise Blood [item=120462]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- a drogmor [npc=48105]\n- a feral drogmor [npc=48106]\n- a tortoise [npc=48148]\n- a young tortoise [npc=48159]\n- an impaler [npc=48172]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Silwat #2: Our Simple Purpose [quest=7784]\n- Silwat #3: To Whom It May Concern [quest=7785]\n**Era:** | !The Darkened Sea\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Sun Oct 26 04:00:22 2014\nModified: Fri Dec 19 22:15:27 2025 |\n---\n\n**The Darkened Sea Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\nThis solo task is the first in a series of three and begins with a wyvern named Silwat Viltor [npc=47737] ( **click for map image**) on Thuliasaur Island.\n_Pre-Requisites for Requesting:_\n\\- Minimum Level 95\n_Note: Silwat Viltor only speaks Elder Dragon (90+ skill level required in order to converse with him). Without speaking Elder Dragon, you see:_\nSilwat Viltor appears to have no idea what you are saying.\n_At 90+ Elder Dragon (trainable at guildmasters, if you're needing it), he'll speak with you._\n_Say \"what\" to request the task._\nSilwat Viltor looks at you through ancient glassy eyes. You suddenly take note of the wyvern's skin which shares the texture of aged stone, cracked and brittle. He looms his head closer to yours before speaking, his voice sounds strained as if each word he utters is a struggle, '\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_, long I have yearned to hear my language echoed back to me. These, children, some call them lesser. They cannot share the gift of conversation but they cry out, anguished, terrified.' He breathes heavily, 'You, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_! You must do [what] I cannot, for their sake.'\nYou say, 'What is that?'\nSilwat Viltor turns his gaze to the drogmors across the river, 'They suffer, their aggression is the symptom of a greater disease. You must go from here, gather these things and return. Together', he pauses, taking another deep breath, 'together we will help them.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Aiding the Ailing'.\nSilwat Viltor, a surprisingly ancient wyvern, needs you to collect a few ingredients to concoct an antidote to treat the ailing drogmors.\nThe docile tortoises that roam the Kromtus fishing cove exhibit a long natural life and even temperament. Although the death of one creature to save another makes for an elaborate moral quandary, Silwat's concerns are with the drogmors. Extract a bit of tortoise blood.\nThe ferocious swordfish that swim in the deep waters of the Kromtus fishing cove exhibit a liveliness that Silwat hopes to utilize in curing the drogmors. Extract a bit of impaler blood.\nThe final component Silwat requires for his elixir is a few strands of Riverweed. This plant can be found at the bottom of the ponds formed by rivers around the island. Submerge yourself in the ponds on the interior of the island and forage for some Riverweed.\n\n---\n\n!\n\n---\n\nExtract the blood of a freshly slain tortoise 0/1 (Thuliasaur Island)\n_Kill \"tortoise\" mobs until you receive an \"Unusual Tortoise Blood\"._\nExtract blood from freshly slain impalers 0/2 (Thuliasaur Island)\n_Kill \"an impaler\" mobs until you have 2x \"Discolored Swordfish Blood\"._\nForage some riverweed from the nearby waters 0/1 (Thuliasaur Island)\n_\"Riverweed\" supposedly can be foraged in the deeper waters of the river in the central of the zone, but it can also be foraged on land._\n_Known locations are: +448 +1689, make sure you are submerged in the water._\n_The vicinity of Lyirae Oakwynd's roaming area has been known to work as well._\n_You don't have to forage it yourself, a forager friend can give it to you and it will update this step._\n\n---\n\nDeliver the components to Silwat 0/1 (Thuliasaur Island)\n_Hand in all four items at once to Silwat Viltor to receive a \"Simple Antibody Concoction\"._\nSilwat Viltor gazes upon your reflection in the water, 'Your hasty return reinforces my confidence in your resolve, perhaps I was too quick to judge you, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. Set the ingredients down here in the water.'\nYou set the ingredients down in the water at the old wyvern's feet. He stares intently at them and the water begins to stir. A flash of light emanating from Silwat's feet blinds you for a moment. As your vision returns a small vial bobs gently where the loose ingredients once stirred. You grab the vial, knowing what you must do next.\n\n---\n\nSedate and inoculate a drogmor 0/1 (Thuliasaur Island)\n_Task Window Says:_ Given the erratic behavior the drogmors have been presenting lately it is not likely that you will be able to deliver the antidote to it without first weakening it. Do your best to avoid killing the creature as you weaken it then apply a bit of the antibody around its head, hopefully that will be enough to calm the creature back to its natural docility.\n_DPS any drogmor down to 40% health, and right-click the concoction to update._\n_Emote If Too Soon:_ The drogmor trashes violently. You'll need to weaken it a bit more before giving it the antibody.\n_Emote Update:_ You splash the antibody over the drogmor's face. It snaps angrily at you at first but after mere moments it grows increasingly amiable. It emits a low peaceful roar in your direction before turning and running away into the jungle.\n\n---\n\nReturn to Silwat Viltor 0/1 (Thuliasaur Island)\n_Task Window Says:_ Let Silwat Viltor know you were successful in curing at least one of the ailing drogmors.\n_Make sure your language is set to Elder Dragon. or try hail him in common, NOT elder dragon._\nYou say, 'Hail, Silwat Viltor'\nThe skin around the ancient wyvern's mouth grinds like fractured stone as he beams with the beginnings of a smile. He slowly turns his gaze toward the remaining drogmors, pleased to know that their suffering will eventually be mitigated.\nSilwat Viltor is pleased with your assistance and will likely have more work for you when you are ready.\n_Rewards:_\nSkeletal Parrot's Synsacrum --OR-- 50 platinum\n_Task repeatability isn't known: You may only be able to repeat by redoing the series after completion, but this isn't known for sure._\n- Skeletal Parrot's Synsacrum [item=120446]",
